WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.920
As a teacher, you have a lot of work to do,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.860
and a lot of content to deliver.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.340
In this video, I will take you on a journey

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.340
right from the start where you get your time table

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.720
or your learning objective,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.380
to how you could use different Google Classroom tools

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.920
to teach your students online

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.800
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.580
As a teacher, assume that I have to teach

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.780
the following concept to my students.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.620
And there are additional details given as well.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.720
Pause the video, take a moment

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.080
and go through the text you see on the screen

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.360
Now I have to think of 3 broad things.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.320
1st,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.140
What is it that my students need to know in advance;

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.060
2nd, what is it that I

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.340
will teach during the live class,

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.780
and third,

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.340
How is it that I will check for their understanding.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.900
As simple as that!

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.600
So how will I begin?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.020
I create a class….

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.160
fill in the required details…

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.240
and click on create...

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.940
It will get us to this screen!

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.160
Please note that some teachers may

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.340
create a class differently.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.760
Here I've created one Google Classroom class

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.500
to teach one subject to one class.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.980
As a teacher it depends on what you're comfortable

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.460
with and what your school requests you to do.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.680
If you remember,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.400
the name of the chapter was Quadrilaterals.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.440
So let me go to the ClassWork section,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.180
click on create,

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.340
and create the topic called Quadrilaterals.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.660
Now this becomes a chapter within my class!

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.900
Now let me go back to the stream section of my class.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.720
Once my class is created,

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.720
I will share the Class code you see here

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.420
with my students.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.440
My students will then use the Join Class option

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.280
to enter the code and join my class.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.840
Maybe I could first make an announcement for

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.660
the students about the live class by posting

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.600
it on the Stream like this…

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.000
or I could also send out an email to all my students

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.060
by going to the People Section.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.900
Before I start communicating with my students, it's

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.200
important that I have done my homework as a teacher.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.520
It’s always a good idea to keep your presentations,

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.500
files, images, and questions ready.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.060
But where could I store these files

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.060
without the risk of losing them?

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.660
The answer is Google Drive!

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.680
Wait, What is that?

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.480
Let me quickly explain.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.440
It’s a place where we can store our files.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.880
And the files are not stored on our local machine

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.480
or laptop here

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.740
It’s stored on remote servers,

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.740
which is a much safer option,

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.720
and we can access it whenever we feel like.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.780
The data there is completely safe

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.120
and no one can really access our files unless we give

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.800
anyone the permission to access them!

00:02:53.809 --> 00:02:54.870
But…

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.209
How do I access Google Drive in Google Classroom?

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:01.020
All I will do is go to the Classwork section,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.040
and here I can see the Class Drive Folder button.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.940
Let me click on it.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.820
This space I am seeing here is where I can save my files

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.540
and access them whenever I wish to.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.040
If I go to Classroom here,

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.680
I will see folders for all the classes I am managing

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.380
or the ones that I had managed before.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.920
Let me get into the current class folder.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.160
Now how do I Add files here?

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.740
After I use the right-click option,

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.740
there are 2 things I can do.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.520
One, I could also ADD my files or folders here

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.200
by simply using the Upload options.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.000
This will allow me to upload my existing files

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.380
from my machine to this folder.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.620
It’s as easy as that.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.040
And second,

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.040
I could directly CREATE files

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.340
by using any of the other options.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.320
I could create a Google Doc,

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.220
a Google Slides Presentation,

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.220
or even a Google Form for quizzes.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.360
And don’t worry;

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.020
my students will NOT have access to this folder,

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.580
unless I give it to them.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.700
Once I have all the files ready

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.260
for my pre-class and post-class work,

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.700
I am now ready to begin

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:15.140
using the Google Classroom tools to teach my students.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.040
And I don’t have to worry as I can

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.280
always Add or Remove more files on the go!

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.140
At this point, I have most of my files ready

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.140
in my Class Drive Folder.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.800
Some preclass files and some postclass files.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.340
Now I have done most of my background work!

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.760
Let us go back to our class in Google Classroom.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.920
By clicking on Create,

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.260
I am ready to share some material with my students.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.600
I enter the title and the description,

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.260
and then give students access to the relevant

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.000
files I have created.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.740
We click on Add, and then go to Google Drive!

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.400
Now, this is interesting!

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.380
In the recent tab, I will be able to see which files

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:03.039
I recently created or uploaded to Google Drive.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.700
If it’s something I created recently,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.020
it will be very easy to select one from here.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.820
But there’s an even better way.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:13.020
If I remember the name of my file,

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.020
I could just SEARCH for it here,

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:17.419
and select from the dropdown.

00:05:17.419 --> 00:05:19.889
Let me select one now.

00:05:19.889 --> 00:05:23.020
To add another file, I go to Add again,

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.420
And alternatively, I could go to MyDrive,

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:29.980
then to my class, and then select the file.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:33.560
You will see it here along with the previous one.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.800
If I have not kept the files ready,

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.960
I could also create it on the go by clicking on ‘Create’

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.760
and then selecting the most appropriate option!

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.720
Now I am almost ready to post this and

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.500
share it with my students.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.060
I will just select the relevant topic

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.060
and click on Post.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.120
Now the background knowledge topics

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.720
are ready for my students.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.580
I’ve now covered what students need to know in

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.700
advance, that is BEFORE my live class.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.420
In the next video,

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.420
I will show you how I will use different tools

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.780
in Google Classroom to teach during a live class,

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.020
and also how we could check for

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.900
the understanding of our students

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.560
See you there!

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:21.020
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.360
[ YouTube Learning ]

